; expect 41
; MAC-CAP-5's three SCALAR queries, each landing with the library
; macro that needs it (MAC-CAP-6's closure rule: a vocabulary entry
; with no consumer is one nothing measures).
;
;   (syntax/name C)      the constructor's spelling as a String
;                        literal - `stdlib/Pre.ax`'s deriveShow, and
;                        the only way a tag's NAME reaches a running
;                        program (a tag is an integer at run time)
;   (syntax/arity C)     the constructor's field count as an Int
;                        literal - deriveArity, and not derivable at
;                        run time either (MM-VAL-6: a block records
;                        its tag, never its field count)
;   (syntax/defined n)   whether `n` names a visible declaration,
;                        DECIDED AT EXPANSION TIME so the losing
;                        branch is deleted rather than compiled -
;                        showOr, whose taken branch names a
;                        declaration the other program does not have
;
; and the composition the three of them needed:
;
;   ((syntax/join a b) x) calls what a join NAMES. Spines flatten, so
;                        the call arrives as one spine headed by the
;                        query; separating the joined parts from the
;                        call's own arguments is what makes a
;                        generated declaration callable from a macro
;                        rather than only nameable.
;
;   16  strLen (showShape (Rect 1 2))  = 4, times 4
;    9  arityShape (Rect 1 2)          = 2, plus 7
;   12  arityShape (Dot)               = 0, plus 12
;    3  showOr Shape (Dot) -> showShape (Dot) = "Dot", strLen 3
;    1  showOr Colour ... -> the fallback, because no deriveShow
;                            Colour was invoked: strLen "?" = 1
;
; 16 + 9 + 12 + 3 + 1 = 41.
;
; The unfixed compiler refuses at expansion: syntax/name is not in
; its vocabulary (AX3028), exit 1.
(import Pre)
(import Str)

(data Shape
  (Circle Int)
  (Rect Int Int)
  (Dot))

(data Colour
  (Red)
  (Green))

(deriveShow Shape)
(deriveArity Shape)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (+ (* 4 (strLen (showShape (Rect 1 2))))
     (+ (+ 7 (arityShape (Rect 1 2)))
        (+ (+ 12 (arityShape Dot))
           (+ (strLen (showOr Shape Dot "?"))
              (strLen (showOr Colour Red "?")))))))
